WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience cheering and applauding)

2
00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.360
After failing to broker

3
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.440
the purchase of Greenland in Nuuk,

4
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.793
I headed north to give it one last shot.

5
00:00:06.793 --> 00:00:09.630
(dramatic music)

6
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.040 line:15%
This one here.
I brought you

7
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:11.873 line:15%
[Conan] Look.

8
00:00:11.873 --> 00:00:12.800 line:15%
this little girl.

9
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.740 line:15%
Oh my God.

10
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.235
Not to keep, obviously.

11
00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:17.068
No, sorry.

12
00:00:17.068 --> 00:00:18.600
(audience laughing)

13
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.442
(child giggling)

14
00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:21.113
Oh, you got me!

15
00:00:22.394 --> 00:00:23.227
(exclaiming)

16
00:00:23.227 --> 00:00:24.060
(child giggling)

17
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.670
You like that one, you like that one.

18
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.163
Wow, look at that.

19
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.110
And there's a cruise ship.

20
00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.663
Everyone on that cruise ship has diarrhea.

21
00:00:32.663 --> 00:00:34.300
(child giggling)

22
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.425
(audience laughing)

23
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:37.708
That is incredible.

24
00:00:37.708 --> 00:00:39.680 line:15%
I don't think I've seen an iceberg before.

25
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.680 line:15%
They used to be bigger.

26
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.470 line:15%
About 20 years ago they were three times bigger than now.

27
00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:47.780 line:15%
Temperatures this July

28
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.120
smashed heat records across the globe,

29
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.860
and the impact was particularly tough on Greenland.

30
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.710 line:15%
Nearly half of Greenland's ice sheet

31
00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.280 line:15%
began melting this week

32
00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.450 line:15%
after an unprecedented warm spell hit the arctic region.

33
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.167
Temperatures were more than 40 degrees above average.

34
00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.590
[Helicopter Reporter] There's enough ice in Greenland

35
00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:07.000 line:15%
to raise sea levels by 25 feet world wide.

36
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.180 line:15%
If unprecedented changes are not made, and made soon,

37
00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.916 line:15%
there will be irreversible damage to the planet.

38
00:01:14.916 --> 00:01:15.833
Ah.

39
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:16.666
Broke again!

40
00:01:16.666 --> 00:01:19.416
(child giggling)

41
00:02:10.086 --> 00:02:12.560
With just an hour left before my flight home,

42
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.503
I was finally able to buy some waterfront property.

43
00:02:18.112 --> 00:02:19.703
Okay, you get your ice.

44
00:02:19.703 --> 00:02:21.073
We're getting really close, this is cool.

45
00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:23.425
This is the dumbest thing we've ever done.

46
00:02:23.425 --> 00:02:24.875
(audience laughing)

47
00:02:24.875 --> 00:02:27.708
(dramatic music)

48
00:02:31.555 --> 00:02:32.805
There's no way.

49
00:02:39.598 --> 00:02:41.320 line:15%
It's not even going in.

50
00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.998 line:15%
Oh wait, there's a little crack right here.

51
00:02:43.998 --> 00:02:45.447 line:15%
Oh props, (beep) props.

52
00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.981 line:15%
(audience laughing)

53
00:02:48.981 --> 00:02:53.231
(audience laughing and applauding)

54
00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.000
It just occurred to me,

55
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.040
it'd be funny if this is how the Titanic sank,

56
00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.674
they were trying to get a gag iceberg shot,

57
00:03:01.674 --> 00:03:03.290
(audience laughing)

58
00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.136
and they got too close.

59
00:03:05.136 --> 00:03:05.969 line:15%
(dramatic music)

60
00:03:05.969 --> 00:03:07.510 line:15%
Here we go!

61
00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:08.343 line:15%
Ready?

62
00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.053
Oh, we're already drifting away.

63
00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.270
We've gotta go back.

64
00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:17.470
I need to get down here.

65
00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.111 line:15%
(dramatic music)

66
00:03:21.111 --> 00:03:23.930 line:15%
(audience laughing)

67
00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:24.763
Back!

68
00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:30.953
Dammit!

69
00:03:30.953 --> 00:03:31.786
(audience laughing and clapping)

70
00:03:31.786 --> 00:03:33.552
Don't let it fall.

71
00:03:33.552 --> 00:03:34.823
The sign's falling apart.

72
00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:36.570
It's not gonna stay.

73
00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.610 line:15%
Do we have anything to fix this?

74
00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.612 line:15%
All right, let's go!

75
00:03:39.612 --> 00:03:42.362 line:15%
(dramatic music)

76
00:03:46.579 --> 00:03:47.412
(upbeat music)

77
00:03:47.412 --> 00:03:50.412
(audience cheering)

78
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.776 line:15%
No icebergs were injured in the making of this video.

79
